# Planar herringbone (chevron-fold) mixer.
#
# Nine chevron legs in three staggered groups. Each group biases the run to one
# side and the bias REVERSES between groups — the planar equivalent of the
# alternating half-cycles in a staggered herringbone mixer. Repeatedly
# reorienting the flow stretches and folds the interface, so the diffusion
# distance shrinks geometrically rather than linearly. Mixes in far less length
# than a plain serpentine, at the cost of sharper corners and more pressure.
#
# CAVEAT, and say this to the user: the published staggered herringbone mixer
# works by ridges cut into the channel FLOOR — sub-channel features a planar
# graph at a single Z cannot express. This folds the interface by turning the
# whole channel instead of driving a helical secondary flow. Expect useful
# mixing, not the original device's numbers.
#
# --- the coordinate scheme, so you can re-cut it to any chip -----------------
#
#   centre    cx        = 15        (chip width / 2)
#   amplitude a         = 3.5       (half the side-to-side swing)
#   bias      b(group)  = -1.5, +1.5, -1.5   (reverses every group)
#   legs      3 per group, rise 5 mm each, so 15 mm per group
#
#   leg k of a group (k = 1, 2, 3), starting downward from that group's top y:
#       sign = -1 for odd k, +1 for even k
#       x    = cx + b + sign * a
#       y    = groupTopY - 5 * k
#
# Which gives x ∈ {10, 13, 17, 20} and the nine legs below. Widen the swing by
# raising `a`; fold harder by adding groups, not by adding legs to a group.

chip "Herringbone mixer"
printer standard-4k
size 30 x 76
base 4
wall 2
edge-spacing 3
split two-piece at 2
channel 0.8 x 0.5 rect

port inletA at 10,70 luer-slip inlet water 10
port inletB at 20,70 luer-slip inlet water 10
port outlet at 15,8  luer-slip outlet

node junction at 15,65
path inletA -> junction
path inletB -> junction

# Group 1 — bias -1.5, so the run leans left
path junction -> (10,60) -> (17,55) -> (10,50)
# Group 2 — bias +1.5, the fold reverses
  -> (13,45) -> (20,40) -> (13,35)
# Group 3 — bias -1.5, and reverses back
  -> (10,30) -> (17,25) -> (10,20)
# Gather onto the axis before the outlet
  -> (15,14) -> outlet
